The word lists in this directory (<locale>.txt.gz) are generated by tools/latinime-words from the AOSP keyboard,
LatinIME, as LineageOS ships it (lineage-23.2): the *.combined.gz word lists in its dictionaries/ directory, the
lists its own binary dictionaries are compiled from. Each keeps the language's 80,000 most frequent words with
their frequencies, and its whitelist corrections; words LatinIME marks possibly offensive are left out.

Each list's last part, the words that most often follow a word (for the next word's suggestions), is counted by the
same tool in the sentences of Tatoeba (https://tatoeba.org, the per-language exports of 21 November 2026), as
LatinIME's own dictionaries ship without such pairs. Only the counts are kept, of words the list has, no sentence.
